    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0222",
      "sequence": 234,
      "meaning": "Seeing Rāma’s beauty, one woman said, ‘This is the bridegroom suited to Jānakī. Friend, if the king sees him, let him abandon the vow and resolutely arrange the marriage.’ Another said the king had recognized and respectfully honored the boys with the sage, yet would not abandon his vow and by fate persisted in unwise obstinacy. Another said, ‘If Providence is good and truly gives everyone a fitting reward, then Jānakī will receive this bridegroom—there is no doubt here, friend. If fate brings about such a union, everyone will be fulfilled. Our deep concern, friend, is that by this relationship they might sometimes return. Otherwise, hear me, even their sight will remain far from us; such a meeting occurs only when abundant merit was earned before.’",
