    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0223",
      "sequence": 235,
      "meaning": "Another replied, ‘Friend, you have spoken well; this marriage would greatly benefit everyone.’ Someone objected, ‘Śiva’s bow is hard, and this dark boy has a tender body.’ While all remained uncertain, another said gently, ‘Friend, some say they have great power although they look small. By the dust that touched his lotus feet, Ahalyā, burdened with grave sin, crossed over. Would he then remain without breaking Śiva’s bow? Do not abandon this conviction even by mistake. The same Brahmā who fashioned and adorned Sītā thoughtfully fashioned this dark bridegroom for her.’ Hearing her words they all rejoiced, softly saying, ‘May it be exactly so.’ Groups of lovely-faced, fine-eyed women delighted in their hearts and showered flowers; wherever the two brothers went there was supreme joy.",
