    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0224",
      "sequence": 236,
      "meaning": "The two brothers went to the city’s eastern side, where ground had been prepared for the bow-sacrifice. A broad, beautiful, smoothly plastered arena held a clean, handsomely decorated altar. On every side huge golden platforms had been built for the kings to sit. Behind them, close by on all sides, shone another circle of platforms, somewhat higher and attractive in every way, where townspeople could sit. Near these stood large, lovely white pavilions made in many colors, where women could sit and watch in places appropriate to their respective families. The city’s boys courteously described each arrangement and showed it to the Lord. Using this pretext, all the children, overcome by love, touched his enchanting body; they thrilled with immense joy as they gazed again and again at the brothers.",
