    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0225",
      "sequence": 237,
      "meaning": "Rāma knew that all the children were overcome by love, and they eagerly described each place. Each called the brothers according to his own interest, and the two went affectionately with them. In soft, sweet, captivating words Rāma pointed the arrangements out to his younger brother. He whose māyā creates hosts of worlds in a fraction of an instant at his command now, from compassion for devotees, gazed in wonder at the bow-sacrifice hall. After seeing the spectacle they started back to the guru, inwardly afraid they had delayed. He from fear of whom fear itself is afraid displayed the influence of devotion. Speaking pleasant, gentle words, they reluctantly dismissed the boys. With reverence, love, humility and deep reserve, the brothers bowed their heads at the teacher’s lotus feet and sat with permission.",
